Hi folks.

I've been reading the posts on the newsgroups for a while and I know that there have been a lot of questions about Acclaim's Magic: The Gathering game. I'm a member of Acclaim's Magic: The Gathering - Battlemage team and I'd like to try to answer a few qu
estions where I can.  (I and the rest of the team are HUGE Magic fans, so getting the chance to work on this game has been a big thrill for us. We're also very proud of this game and want everyone to know about it.)

Acclaim's Magic: The Gathering - Battlemage is a real-time strategy game in the tradition of Command and Conquer and Warcraft II, and is based on the fantasy-adventure world of Magic: The Gathering, .What Acclaim's game does is bring the creatures, artifa
cts, and spells of the fantasy adventure world of M:TG to life by drawing on the Magic: The Gathering mechanics and taking it to a new dimension via computer animation.  It will be a fast strategy game with a top down perspective. The player sees their pl
aneswalker and the creatures they control from a distance above the dueling field that allows them to view details of the fights, but still permits them to see a good portion of their surroundings. The object, of course, is to use your creatures, protecti
ons and spells to attack the other wizard and bring him down to 0 life points. The interactions of the units, instants, enchantments, etc. are inspired by the 4th edition and Mirage sets, (booster sets to follow), and  fit into the real-time format. Up to
 4 players can take the roles of planeswalkers controlling up to 54 different animated units on a 3D rendered battlefield. The game will be playable via network, modem/Internet, and serial cable. 

There's a whole bunch of other features as well, like the Campaign mode, research, diplomacy & stuff, but I don't want to run on too long

Magic: The Gathering - Battlemage is coming in November for Windows95, PlayStation and Saturn. If anyone has any questions about the game, how it works or anything, feel free to ask.




